request: Rename the `watched` field of watchlist items to `seen` everywhere.

governor turn 1: plan -> movie, watchlist-store, watchlist, search, movie-detail, app  (Pure data-field rename: the item field `watched` becomes `seen`. `movie` declares the new `Movie`/`WatchItem` shapes, `watchlist-store` updates item creation/toggling/counting/persistence to `seen`, and consumer units update any field references in code/templates. Public API names (`toggleWatched`, `watchedCount`) and UI text are untouched since the request targets only the item field. Acceptance tests pin the new field name in the type declarations and in the store's add/toggle/count/persist behaviour.)
round 1: owners movie=ok watchlist-store=ok watchlist=rejected search=ok movie-detail=ok app=ok; oracle RED
governor turn 2: plan -> watchlist  (Only the watchlist unit is still red: its template (3 bindings) and one existing test still use the old `watched` field. The owner's requested test edit is a mechanical consequence of the approved rename (assertion must read `.seen`), so approve it and re-issue the rename instruction.)
round 2: owners watchlist=ok; oracle RED
governor turn 3: plan -> watchlist-store  (tsc is green and every unit test passes except my watchlist-store acceptance test: in-memory behaviour is already correct (items carry `seen`, toggleWatched flips it, watchedCount follows), but the persistence round-trip still loses the field — a freshly constructed WatchlistStore returns the saved item with `seen === undefined`. Only the watchlist-store unit is implicated: its persisted payload and/or load path still uses the old key. No exported signatures change, so no other unit needs instruction.)
round 3: owners watchlist-store=ok; oracle GREEN
governor turn 4: accept  (Oracle is green (tsc clean, 45/45 tests pass). Acceptance tests for movie and watchlist-store pin the `watched` -> `seen` rename through add, toggle, persistence, and reload; earlier rounds already migrated the dependent units.)

